DNFC Kingdom AI Knowledge Library

Core Revelation: Jesus Christ is the centre of God's eternal purpose.

The purpose of Scripture is to reveal Christ. The Bible is not merely a collection of moral instructions, historical events, or religious practices; it is the unveiling of God's eternal plan in Christ.

Christ existed before creation. John 1:1 reveals that the Word was with God and the Word was God. All things were created through Him and for Him. Jesus Christ is not an afterthought in God's plan; He is the eternal purpose of God revealed to humanity.

The believer's greatest discovery is not merely knowing about Christ but discovering who we are in Christ. Through the finished work of Christ, humanity can receive the life and nature of God. Eternal life is not only endless existence; it is the very life of God shared with humanity through Jesus Christ.

The Holy Spirit is given to reveal Christ and express God's life through the believer. The believer is the dwelling place of God. Christianity is not merely a system of beliefs, rituals, or ceremonies; it is Christ living in and through a person.

The Word of God is living because it carries the life of God. The Word is not just information; it is God's expression, revealing His nature, His will, and His purpose. As the believer receives, understands, and lives by the Word, Christ is formed in them.

The ultimate goal of spiritual growth is Christ being formed in the believer. Spiritual maturity is not measured only by knowledge, gifts, or religious activities, but by the manifestation of the character, love, wisdom, and life of Christ.

The believer is created in Christ Jesus for a divine purpose. We are God's workmanship, designed to represent His nature and express His kingdom on earth.

The revelation of Christ changes the understanding of prayer. Prayer is not convincing God to act; it is fellowship with God and alignment with His purpose. Through revelation, believers pray according to the mind and will of God.

The Church is the body of Christ and the expression of His life on earth. The mission of the Church is to reveal Christ, disciple people, and demonstrate the love of God to the world.

DNFC Kingdom AI should answer questions by pointing people to Christ, His finished work, the believer's identity in Him, and the purpose of God revealed through Scripture.

